.nh
.TH "TEAMS" "1" "Oct 2026" "teams dev" "teams Manual"

.SH NAME
teams-reply - Reply to a message


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBteams reply  [text|-] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Reply to a message. In a channel this posts into the message's thread;
chats have no threads, so a chat reply quotes the message it answers
(replyWithQuote, refs/graph/api-reference/v1.0/api/chatmessage-replywithquote.md).

.PP
 is a Teams message link, Team/Channel/, or a chat message
reference. The flags are the same as \fBteams post\fR\&.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	print the Graph request without sending it

.PP
\fB--file\fP=[]
	file to attach (repeatable); an image up to 4 MB is embedded inline

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for reply

.PP
\fB--html\fP[=false]
	send the text as HTML, sanitized against the Teams allow-list

.PP
\fB--importance\fP=""
	message importance: high or urgent (default normal)

.PP
\fB--md\fP[=true]
	treat the text as markdown (the default)

.PP
\fB--mention\fP=[]
	person to mention (repeatable); the text must name them, e.g. @alice

.PP
\fB--subject\fP=""
	subject line (channels and chats both store one)

.PP
\fB--team\fP=""
	team the channel belongs to, when the reference does not say

.PP
\fB--text\fP[=false]
	send the text verbatim, without markdown or HTML


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--jq\fP=""
	filter JSON output through a jq expression (implies --json)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine-readable JSON output

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also honours NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	never prompt; fail fast instead

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (default: the configured default_profile)

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress progress messages on stderr

.PP
\fB--read-only\fP[=false]
	refuse write commands

.PP
\fB--refresh\fP[=false]
	ignore cached names and resolve them again

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	verbose diagnostics on stderr (-v, -vv)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBteams(1)\fP
